@@ -0,0 +1,29 @@
+@editor @editor_tiny @javascript
+Feature: Insert accordions in TinyMCE
+  In order to present structured content
+  As a user
+  I need to be able to insert collapsible accordion sections using the TinyMCE Accordion plugin
+
+  Scenario: Insert an accordion from the Insert menu
+    Given I am on the "Profile advanced editing" page logged in as "admin"
+    And I set the field "Description" to "<p>Some text</p>"
+    When I click on the "Insert > Accordion" menu item for the "Description" TinyMCE editor
+    And I switch to the "Description" TinyMCE editor iframe
+    Then "details.mce-accordion" "css_element" should exist
+    And "details.mce-accordion summary.mce-accordion-summary" "css_element" should exist
+    And I should see "Accordion summary..." in the "details.mce-accordion summary" "css_element"
+    And I should see "Accordion body..." in the "details.mce-accordion" "css_element"
+
+  Scenario: Accordion content is preserved when saved and displayed
+    Given I am on the "Profile advanced editing" page logged in as "admin"
+    And I set the field "Description" to multiline:
+    """
+    <details class="mce-accordion" open="open">
+      <summary class="mce-accordion-summary">My accordion summary</summary>
+      <p>My accordion body</p>
+    </details>
+    """
+    When I press "Update profile"
+    Then "details.mce-accordion" "css_element" should exist
+    And I should see "My accordion summary" in the "details.mce-accordion summary" "css_element"
+    And I should see "My accordion body" in the "details.mce-accordion" "css_element"
