+@editor @editor_tiny @javascript
+Feature: Apply list styles in TinyMCE
+  In order to format document-style content
+  As a user
+  I need to be able to apply extended list styles using the TinyMCE List Styles plugin
+
+  Scenario: Apply a lower alpha style to a numbered list
+    Given I am on the "Profile advanced editing" page logged in as "admin"
+    And I set the field "Description" to "<ol><li>First item</li><li>Second item</li></ol>"
+    And I expand all toolbars for the "Description" TinyMCE editor
+    And I select the "li" element in position "0" of the "Description" TinyMCE editor
+    When I click on ".tox-split-button__chevron" "css_element" in the "[aria-label='Numbered list']" "css_element"
+    And I click on "[aria-label='Lower Alpha'][role^='menuitem']" "css_element"
+    And I switch to the "Description" TinyMCE editor iframe
+    Then "ol[style*='lower-alpha']" "css_element" should exist
+
+  Scenario: Apply a circle style to a bullet list
+    Given I am on the "Profile advanced editing" page logged in as "admin"
+    And I set the field "Description" to "<ul><li>First item</li><li>Second item</li></ul>"
+    And I expand all toolbars for the "Description" TinyMCE editor
+    And I select the "li" element in position "0" of the "Description" TinyMCE editor
+    When I click on ".tox-split-button__chevron" "css_element" in the "[aria-label='Bullet list']" "css_element"
+    And I click on "[aria-label='Circle'][role^='menuitem']" "css_element"
+    And I switch to the "Description" TinyMCE editor iframe
+    Then "ul[style*='circle']" "css_element" should exist
